Negative control for forced-state.spec.ts (T3.12, AC8.1 · S12).

The revalidation that makes a preset visible must not fire for the preset a tab
already has. `reconcile` is watched with `immediate: true`, so it runs once on
every bare load with Live — and Live is what a booting tab already is. Without
the `next === served` guard that first run drops every answer the page has just
fetched and re-issues them, so a page nobody forced anything on re-reads itself
on boot: a doubled request for every module on the page, and a visible flash of
its own loading state.

This mutant removes the guard alone. The worker still never registers on a bare
load (`AC8.1` is untouched), which is why this is a control the eager-worker one
cannot stand in for: the defect here is a re-read nobody asked for, not an import.

Apply from the repo root: `git apply <this file>`; revert with `git apply -R`.

Reds: forced-state.spec.ts — the case proving a bare load re-reads nothing.

